<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The half mark: "part of the way, or worth an eye."

    Two paths, exactly as InkJudgment.PARTIAL / WeekMark.HALF_DOT draw it: the
    left half fills at the full radius (the Canvas original clips right of
    centre and draws a whole circle), and then the outline closes the circle
    "so the missing half reads as unfinished rather than as a smaller dot" —
    the glyph file's own words, and the reason this is not just a scaled dot.

    The closing outline is an even-odd FILLED annulus (outer edge 6, inner edge
    4.15 — the centreline at the source's `radius - hairline / 2f` = 5.075 with
    stroke 1.85), not a stroked circle: the first device build lost every
    stroked path while the filled mark drew fine, which left this one reading
    as a plain dot. Fill-only geometry rides the code path the working mark
    proves. The 1.85/12 ring thickness is within 0.05dp of BOTH source ratios
    (1.4dp/9dp judgment glyph, 1.2dp/8dp tally dot), which is what lets one
    drawable set serve both sizes.

    The authored colour is IRRELEVANT: every use site draws this through
    ColorFilter.tint(ColorProvider), which is how the one-ink rule survives into
    a surface that cannot read LogbookTheme.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="12dp"
    android:height="12dp"
    android:viewportWidth="12"
    android:viewportHeight="12">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M6,0 A6,6 0 0,0 6,12 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M6,6 m-6,0 a6,6 0 1,0 12,0 a6,6 0 1,0 -12,0 M6,6 m-4.15,0 a4.15,4.15 0 1,0 8.3,0 a4.15,4.15 0 1,0 -8.3,0" />
</vector>
